[{"id":126011,"sender_id":1436,"sender_full_name":"kirk_sturtz","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91e997b15d87114e342396840b7aed6f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Giry.20monad/near/126011\">#91</a> In referencing Lawvere’s original appendix publication I have switched that pointer to the version which was Latex’ed up by several researchers.  This switch was made because that version includes Commentary by the Author in July 2020 which directly relates to generalized points, and in particular to weakly averaging functionals. Moreover, everyone is probably more interested in the commentary more that the original write-up (which is marked up) because everyone has already read Giry’s paper. I retained the reference to the original document I found at AIM in 2002.</p>\n<p>I added the linearity condition to the definition of a generalized point which makes Lemma 3.2 self-evident.  Also, the last theorem was incomplete so I split it into a Lemma showing fullness, and the conjecture on Every affine map from an algebra to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}_{\\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">R</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is measurable.  Given that I have thought about this monad since 2002, I can assure you I am working on its completion!</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Giry+monad/120\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Giry+monad/120\">v120</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Giry+monad\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1788655221,"subject":"Giry monad","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126038,"sender_id":1436,"sender_full_name":"kirk_sturtz","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/91e997b15d87114e342396840b7aed6f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/Giry.20monad/near/126038\">#92</a> I used Beck’s <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/monadicity%20theorem\">monadicity theorem</a> to prove that the comparison functor <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s</mi></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Meas}_{\\mathrm{Cvx}} \\rightarrow \\mathbf{Meas}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8361em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Meas</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">Cvx</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9173em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Meas</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9173em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.139em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">G</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is an isomorphism.  </p>\n<p>In stepping through the proof I realized that the definition of the category <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s</mi></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Meas} \\cap \\mathbf{Cvx}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Meas</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∩</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Cvx</span></span></span></span></span>, and hence the category <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Meas}_{\\mathrm{Cvx}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8361em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Meas</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3283em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">Cvx</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, had to include the vital condition that all the affine sum operations must be measurable functions. So that has been added to the definition.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/diff/Giry+monad/127\">diff</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/revision/Giry+monad/127\">v127</a>, <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Giry+monad\">current</a></p>","timestamp":1789385552,"subject":"Giry monad","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]